<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Mana Points</h1>
<p>Mana is the energy you spend to cast spells; each spell costs its own 
amount (shown in its help). With too little mana left, you can't cast. 
<a cmd='#'>score</a> shows how much you have of your most.
</p><p><b>How much you can have.</b> 100, plus half the sum of your brain and 
charisma, up to 200 at most. It also grows as your character ages, up to 
two fifths more late in life, and it fades away when you grow too old 
for your race (see <a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>).
</p><p><b>Getting it back.</b> Mana comes back by itself every half minute, 
except while you fight:
</p>
<ul><li>the more mana you can hold, the faster it comes;</li>
<li>charisma matters most: when your charisma is higher than both your magic and your divine, it comes back faster, and when lower, more slowly;</li>
<li>half again as fast when you rest or sleep, a quarter faster when you sit, and twice as fast in holy places (see <a cmd='#'>Help Regenerate</a>);</li>
<li>hunger and thirst slow it down.</li></ul>
<p>A sorcerer can give you mana with <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Boost</a>, and some potions 
restore it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Regenerate</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Charisma</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Magic</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Boost</a>
</pre>




</div>